<Deck title="The Next Token" brand="NEXT TOKEN" series="EPISODE 01 — THE BUILD" chat={true}>
<deck-cue time="STEP 0 · THE MYSTERY" title="The question">Open on the premise, then the meme: the models said two, it is three, two camps formed overnight. Land the join: both camps argued about the answer — nobody asked what the machine was looking at. We build it, one part at a time.</deck-cue>
<deck-cue time="STEP 1 · ITS EYES" title="Part 1: eyes">It never saw letters: chunks and numbers, slices that do not align with letters. The JPEG line: the information is in there, practically unreadable. Replay the slice on "chunks". Hand-off: so what does it do with them?</deck-cue>
<deck-cue time="STEP 2 · ONE MOVE, THEN THE LOOP" title="Parts 2–3: the move, the loop">The whole move is prediction — it commits to a digit with no counter, guessing what a correct answer looks like. Kill the smuggled definition of intelligence (flawless, internal, one pass). Intelligence is the loop: intent, artifact, reaction, revision. The correction is the thinking.</deck-cue>
<deck-cue time="STEP 3 · THE PARTNER" title="Part 4: the partner">The builder version: the specification emerges while you build. Not an autonomous genius — a high-bandwidth execution partner. Land his diagram line, then the join: "deterministic tools underneath — hold onto that phrase."</deck-cue>
<deck-cue time="STEP 4 · THE ROUTER" title="Part 5: the router">The loop alone spins; intelligence is the routing. Four layers; routing itself can fail. Newsboy as the worked proof: ownership, not emphasis — compute where exact, infer where ambiguous. Civilisation ran the same playbook. Recap beat, then: the machine is built.</deck-cue>
<deck-cue time="STEP 5 · THE CATCH" title="The scoreboard">Slow down. Every loop optimises for something, not always what is written on the box. Goodhart: the measure becomes the target. Point at the machine: the scoreboard was there all along — we just had not labelled it.</deck-cue>
<deck-cue time="STEP 6 · RUNNING US" title="The same machine, running us">Aim it at belief: stated vs revealed preference, badges, insulation, no blame — universal equipment. Then the narrator: the reasons are the press release, the incentives are the process. Gates as the worked example. Climax: build the check outside the thing being checked.</deck-cue>
<deck-cue time="STEP 7 · THE CHECK, ENGINEERED" title="The ledger">The philosophy becomes architecture: plausible is not valid. Where does reality live? Inference proposes, authority decides. Distrust the instrument before the subject. Permission is propose, pause, decide, execute — never one boolean.</deck-cue>
<deck-cue time="STEP 8 · AT SCALE" title="The same machine, at scale">Zoom out: Pareto (records, not speeches), Mosca (the political formula), Michels (the iron law where it should have failed). The funnel: the minority sets the menu. Then money as interface — the monthly payment is not the price.</deck-cue>
<deck-cue time="STEP 9 · CLOSE" title="The machine, assembled">Return to the strawberry, now sliced. That is the show: not the news, the machinery underneath. Final question to camera — what is your loop optimising for, and can anything outside it tell it it is wrong? Hold. End card: The Tool Call Is Not the Plan.</deck-cue>

